--
-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: what a period of time is counted from, and what the
-- rules for counting apply to (s 25(1), s 25(2)). The counting itself (ss 25(3), 25(4), 25.1 to 25.5) is in
-- `bc-interpretation-time.l4`.
--
-- What FALSE and REFUSE mean here (NOTES.md, finding 2). TRUE: the case is within the provision and the provision gives the
-- thing. FALSE: only where the words of the provision give the negative themselves (an exception, "is not", "must ... one
-- whose"). REFUSE: the case is outside what the provision speaks of, or the provision only permits or "includes" and the
-- case is not listed; the text is silent and a default would be a guess.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `s 25(1) Reference day`

DECLARE `What a period of time is counted from` IS ONE OF
    `A specified or implied day`
        HAS `the day specified or implied` IS A DATE
    `A day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs`
        HAS `the day the event or act occurs` IS A DATE
    `A day on which a different period begins or ends`
        HAS `the day the different period begins or ends` IS A DATE
    `Something else`

-- src:154 | 25 (1) In sections 25.2 to 25.4, reference day means any of the following by reference to which the beginning or end of a period of time must be determined:
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(1) (src:154)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(1) defines reference day for sections 25.2 to 25.4 only` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 25(1) defines reference day for sections 25.2 to 25.4 only"

-- src:154 | 25 (1) In sections 25.2 to 25.4, reference day means any of the following by reference to which the beginning or end of a period of time must be determined:
-- src:155 | (a) a specified or implied day;
-- src:156 | (b) a day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs;
-- src:157 | (c) a day on which a different period begins or ends.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(1) (src:154-157)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(1) names three kinds of reference day and no others` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 25(1) names three kinds of reference day and no others"

-- "reference day means any of the following": "means" closes the list, so something else is not a reference day.
-- src:154 | 25 (1) In sections 25.2 to 25.4, reference day means any of the following by reference to which the beginning or end of a period of time must be determined:
-- src:155 | (a) a specified or implied day;
-- src:156 | (b) a day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs;
-- src:157 | (c) a day on which a different period begins or ends.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(1)(a) to (c) (src:154-157)
GIVEN counted IS A `What a period of time is counted from`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) a thing a period is counted from is a reference day` counted MEANS
    CONSIDER counted
        WHEN `A specified or implied day` d THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs` d THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A day on which a different period begins or ends` d THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Something else` THEN FALSE

-- src:154 | 25 (1) In sections 25.2 to 25.4, reference day means any of the following by reference to which the beginning or end of a period of time must be determined:
-- src:155 | (a) a specified or implied day;
-- src:156 | (b) a day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs;
-- src:157 | (c) a day on which a different period begins or ends.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(1)(a) to (c) (src:154-157)
GIVEN counted IS A `What a period of time is counted from`
      `the question is asked in section 25.2, 25.3 or 25.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(1) the reference day` counted `the question is asked in section 25.2, 25.3 or 25.4` MEANS
    IF   `the question is asked in section 25.2, 25.3 or 25.4`
    THEN CONSIDER counted
             WHEN `A specified or implied day` d THEN d
             WHEN `A day on which a specified or implied event or act occurs` d THEN d
             WHEN `A day on which a different period begins or ends` d THEN d
             WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 25(1) names three kinds of reference day and no others`
    ELSE `s 25(1) defines reference day for sections 25.2 to 25.4 only`

§ `s 25(2) Deeds, conveyances and other legal instruments`

DECLARE `Kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `A deed`
    `A conveyance`
    `Another legal instrument`
    `Not a legal instrument`

-- src:158 | (2) This section and sections 25.1 to 25.5 also apply to a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument unless specifically provided otherwise in the deed, conveyance or other legal instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(2) (src:158)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) speaks only of a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 25(2) speaks only of a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument"

-- src:158 | (2) This section and sections 25.1 to 25.5 also apply to a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument unless specifically provided otherwise in the deed, conveyance or other legal instrument.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 25(2) (src:158)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of document`
      `the instrument specifically provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) section 25 and sections 25.1 to 25.5 apply to the document` kind `the instrument specifically provides otherwise` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `A deed` THEN NOT `the instrument specifically provides otherwise`
        WHEN `A conveyance` THEN NOT `the instrument specifically provides otherwise`
        WHEN `Another legal instrument` THEN NOT `the instrument specifically provides otherwise`
        WHEN `Not a legal instrument` THEN `s 25(2) speaks only of a deed, conveyance or other legal instrument`
